# Prototype presets

This plugin is still a prototype. DAW sessions and host automation are reset with each update. They are not a compatibility target.

- User presets are plain text with a format version (`dsp/include/subdoom/PresetIO.h`). Reading tolerates unknown and missing keys; that is tolerance, not migration. Do not add migration, old-format branches, or spare slots so a previously saved file still loads.
- Add, remove, or reorder parameters when the sound needs it. Update the table in `dsp/include/subdoom/Parameters.h`, the factory table in `FactoryPresets.cpp`, and any test that names the current set in the same change.
- Factory presets compiled into the plugin are the current sounds. Edit them freely. Do not keep a behavior so a previously saved slot still matches.
